  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, scgpt, transformer) achieved 0.514 acc, outperforming config_010 (multimodal, scgpt, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.471 acc. The 4.3-point drop when adding the image modality via concat fusion suggests the combination strategy may be the bottleneck rather than the image features themselves. Question: Does switching from concat to weighted fusion (config_038) recover multimodal performance, isolating whether the fusion mechanism is the issue while keeping all other settings (scgpt, resnet50, transformer, multiprofile) identical to config_010? Why this is the best next step: It is a clean single-variable comparison with config_010, directly testing the most likely cause of the multimodal underperformance. If weighted fusion helps, it opens a promising multimodal direction for exploitation in remaining experiments; if it does not, it strengthens the case that resnet50 image features are uninformative here, redirecting effort toward RNA-only improvements or a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) in subsequent trials."
}

